//BUG="a comment line adds its own indentation to the line below it"
//OUT="other"

// The same defect as 44, seen from the other side. A line comment eats the
// newline that ends it (`Location::SingleLineComment` in
// src/compiler/preprocessor.rs), so a line that holds nothing but a comment
// does not disappear: its leading spaces stay behind and are glued in front of
// the next line. Here that is 4 + 4 = 8 spaces before `else`, which puts the
// `else` inside the body of the `if` it belongs to, and the compile fails with
// "Unexpected token" pointing at `else`.
//
// Commenting the branches of an if/else like this is about as ordinary as
// code gets. Moving the comment to column 0 is the only spelling that works
// today, because then it has no indentation to leak.

fn main
    x = 2
    if x == 1
        out "one"
    // anything else
    else
        out "other"
